voidwolf live image
==================

Identity
--------
- Hostname: voidwolf
- Session: startx → XLibre → dwm (no greeter / display manager)
- Base: Void Linux glibc x86_64 (first target)
- FDE: not provided by voidwolf; pre-configure LUKS if you need it

Live session
------------
1. Log in (credentials printed at boot / set by mklive user args).
2. If voidwolf-suckless is installed: `export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"` only needed
   when you rebuild user-local themed binaries.
3. `startx`
4. Super+Return = st, Super+Space = launcher, Super+Shift+B = browser (if installed)

Local packages
--------------
If this image embedded packages/repo, xbps may list voidwolf-* packages.
  xbps-query -Rs voidwolf

Post-install (target disk)
--------------------------
1. Install Void base (void-installer or manual).
2. Clone or copy this repo, or install from your local XBPS repo.
3. ./bootstrap/repos.sh && ./bootstrap/bootstrap.sh --profile desktop --gpu … --with-suckless
   OR: xbps-install voidwolf-desktop voidwolf-helpers voidwolf-suckless + install-dotfiles.sh
4. Enable elogind, re-login, startx.

NVIDIA
------
Discrete: --gpu nvidia + nvidia-setup.sh (see docs/nvidia.md).
Hybrid: --gpu nvidia-hybrid | nvidia-hybrid-randr.

Brave
-----
Not on the live image by default. After vw-repo:
  sudo xbps-install -y brave-origin   # or brave-origin-bin

